rem dp.pnx - basic bench `dp`: edit distance of two strings of n letters (a c g t as 0 to 3) from linear generators, in two
rem rolling rows. pnx dp.pnx N (default 1500, up to 4000).
use io .
use env .
use str .
const most 4001
array a int most
array b int most
array prev int most
array cur int most
def main or fail do
  1 env.arg or_else to e "1500" end str.to_int or_fail to n
  0 n range do to i
    i 2654435761 mul 13 shr 3 bit_and i set a
    i 40503 mul 7 add 11 shr 3 bit_and i set b
  end each
  0 n 1 add range do to j j j set prev end each
  1 to i
  loop
    i n le not if break . end
    i 0 set cur
    i 1 sub a idx to ai
    1 to k
    loop
      k n le not if break . end
      k prev idx 1 add to best
      k 1 sub cur idx 1 add to ins
      ins best lt if ins to best end
      ai  k 1 sub b idx ne if 1 else 0 end to cost
      k 1 sub prev idx cost add to sbc
      sbc best lt if sbc to best end
      best k set cur
      k 1 add to k
    end
    0 n 1 add range do to t t cur idx t set prev end each
    i 1 add to i
  end
  args "dp " n " " n prev idx . cat io.println
end
main or_else to e args "dp: " e err_text . cat io.println end
